---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";

const sections = [
  { id: "agreement", label: "Agreement and eligibility" },
  { id: "service", label: "The service" },
  { id: "accounts", label: "Accounts and security" },
  { id: "acceptable-use", label: "Acceptable use" },
  { id: "content", label: "Content and ownership" },
  { id: "third-parties", label: "Third-party services" },
  { id: "availability", label: "Availability" },
  { id: "disclaimers", label: "Disclaimers and liability" },
  { id: "termination", label: "Termination" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes and contact" },
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
	title="Terms of service | Livefeed"
	description="Terms governing use of the Livefeed CLI, website, and authentication service."
	heading="Terms of service"
	summary="These terms govern the Livefeed command-line application, website, and hosted authentication service."
	effectiveDate="25 July 2026"
	active="terms"
	sections={sections}
>
	<section id="agreement">
		<h2>Agreement and eligibility</h2>
		<p>
			By downloading, installing, or using Livefeed, you agree to these terms. If you use
			Livefeed for an organization, you represent that you are authorized to accept these terms
			for that organization.
		</p>
		<p>
			You must be at least 13 years old and legally permitted to use Google, YouTube, Twitch, Kick, and
			Cloudflare services in your location. If applicable law requires a higher minimum age, that
			higher age applies.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="service">
		<h2>The service</h2>
		<p>
			Livefeed is an open-source, read-only terminal client that discovers an active YouTube,
			Twitch, or Kick stream associated with your authorized account and displays its live chat. The
			hosted authentication service keeps provider client secrets out of the distributed CLI.
		</p>
		<p>
			Livefeed does not broadcast video, manage stream settings, send chat messages, guarantee
			chat history, or provide moderation tools. Features may change as provider APIs and the
			open-source project evolve.
		</p>
		<p>
			The current public version is provided without charge. There are no subscriptions,
			automatic renewals, paid plans, or refunds.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="accounts">
		<h2>Accounts and security</h2>
		<p>
			Livefeed does not create a separate Livefeed account. You authenticate using your own
			Google, Twitch, or Kick account. You are responsible for:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>keeping your device and provider accounts secure;</li>
			<li>reviewing the scopes shown during provider authorization;</li>
			<li>using Livefeed only with accounts you are authorized to access; and</li>
			<li>revoking access promptly if a device or credential may be compromised.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Run <code>livefeed logout</code> and choose the relevant provider to revoke and
			remove the corresponding local credential.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="acceptable-use">
		<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
		<p>You may not use Livefeed or its authentication service to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>access an account, stream, or chat without authorization;</li>
			<li>violate law, provider terms, privacy rights, or intellectual-property rights;</li>
			<li>bypass rate limits or probe, overload, disrupt, or degrade the hosted service;</li>
			<li>extract, disclose, or misuse another person’s credentials or private information;</li>
			<li>impersonate the project or misrepresent an unofficial build as an official release;</li>
			<li>introduce malicious code or use automated traffic that materially harms the service; or</li>
			<li>use the OAuth broker as authentication infrastructure for another product.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			These restrictions do not limit rights granted by the project’s open-source license or
			applicable law, including legitimate security research conducted responsibly.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="content">
		<h2>Content and ownership</h2>
		<p>
			You retain your rights in your account information and content. Livefeed claims no
			ownership of chat messages or provider data. The CLI temporarily processes that content
			only to display it on your device.
		</p>
		<p>
			Livefeed’s source code is licensed under the MIT License. The license governs your rights
			to use, copy, modify, and distribute the software. These terms do not grant rights to
			third-party names, logos, APIs, or content.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="third-parties">
		<h2>Third-party services</h2>
		<p>
			Livefeed depends on Google, YouTube, Twitch, Kick, Cloudflare, your operating system’s credential
			manager, npm, and Bun. Your use of those services remains subject to their own terms and
			policies.
		</p>
		<p>
			Use of Livefeed’s YouTube functionality is also subject to the
			<a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and the
			<a href="https://developers.google.com/youtube/terms/api-services-terms-of-service">
				YouTube API Services Terms of Service
			</a>.
		</p>
		<p>
			Provider outages, API changes, revoked credentials, disabled live chat, quota restrictions,
			or changes to third-party terms may interrupt or permanently alter Livefeed. We do not
			control those services and are not responsible for their acts or omissions.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="availability">
		<h2>Availability and support</h2>
		<p>
			Livefeed is provided as an open-source project without a service-level agreement. The CLI,
			website, and authentication service may be unavailable, rate limited, modified, or
			discontinued at any time.
		</p>
		<p>
			Community support and issue reporting are available through the public GitHub repository.
			No response time or resolution is guaranteed.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="disclaimers">
		<h2>Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>
				To the fullest extent permitted by law, Livefeed is provided “as is” and “as available,”
				without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory.
			</strong>
			We do not warrant that Livefeed will be uninterrupted, secure, error-free, compatible with
			every terminal, or able to retrieve every stream or message.
		</p>
		<p>
			To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Livefeed project and its maintainers will not
			be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages,
			or for lost data, revenue, profits, goodwill, or business interruption arising from use of
			the service.
		</p>
		<p>
			Where liability cannot legally be excluded, aggregate liability will not exceed the greater
			of the amount you paid for Livefeed in the twelve months before the claim or USD 10. Some
			jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions or limitations, so these provisions may not
			apply to you. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot be excluded
			under applicable law.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="termination">
		<h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
		<p>
			You may stop using Livefeed at any time and revoke provider access. We may block or limit
			access to the hosted authentication service when reasonably necessary to address abuse,
			security risk, legal requirements, or violations of these terms.
		</p>
		<p>
			Provisions concerning ownership, third-party services, disclaimers, liability, and any
			terms that by their nature should survive will remain effective after use ends.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="changes">
		<h2>Changes, applicable law, and contact</h2>
		<p>
			We may update these terms as Livefeed changes. The effective date will be revised and
			material changes will be documented in the repository. Continued use after an update means
			you accept the revised terms where permitted by law.
		</p>
		<p>
			Applicable law and courts with jurisdiction govern these terms without overriding mandatory
			consumer protections available to you. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining
			provisions remain effective. A failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver.
		</p>
		<p>
			Questions about these terms may be submitted through the
			<a href="https://github.com/DeepanshuMishraa/livefeed/issues">Livefeed issue tracker</a>.
			Do not post credentials or private account information.
		</p>
	</section>
</LegalPage>
